            <div xml:id="d49">

                <pb facs="0067" n="55" sameAs="frus:frus1942v01/pg55"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00116 European War 1939/555: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in the United
                        Kingdom</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Winant</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1942-09-21T22:00:00-04:00">September 21, 1942—10
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>4588. From Hopkins. With reference to your telegram no. 5253,<anchor n="31"
                        xml:id="d49-f1"/> your August 5th letter has just reappeared after having
                    been mislaid. I am in agreement with you that no direct or indirect reference
                    ought to be made to the Bryce Committee. I hope you will receive word very soon
                    on this matter which has been turned over to the State Department.
                    [Hopkins.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
